    <tr><td>Bio</td><td>Public on your public profile and on the pages of the workshops you teach, unless you make it private; a bio written for a workshop shows on that workshop's page</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Event photos, with the name and caption typed</td><td>Public on the event's page when the organiser has opened it to photos; a photo waiting for approval is visible to the moderators and its sender only (see §3bis)</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Reports of a photo and their comments</td><td>Visible to the moderators only</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Your personal schedule, your workshop attendance</td><td>Visible only to you and to the organiser</td></tr>
    <tr><td><strong>Email address</strong></td><td><strong>Never public.</strong> No public interface returns it; the database itself enforces this</td></tr>
