<h2>9. Cookies</h2>
<p>MyClash sets <strong>only its own cookies</strong>, all listed below. None is used for advertising, audience measurement or tracking.</p>
<table>
  <thead><tr><th>Cookie</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Lifetime</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td><code>sb-access-token</code></td><td>Keeps you signed in</td><td>30 days, renewed while you stay active</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>sb-refresh-token</code></td><td>Renews your session without asking you to sign in again</td><td>30 days</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>mc-oauth-…-code-verifier</code></td><td>During a Google sign-in, links the return from Google to the browser that started it; deleted once used</td><td>1 hour</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>mc_guest</code></td><td>Your guest session at an event, when you have no account</td><td>Until 7 days after the event</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>mc_staff</code></td><td>Signs a staff tablet or phone (scoring, check-in desk, gear, photos) in to one event, once its code is entered</td><td>Until 6 am the day after the event's last day; 12 hours for a sign-in made after that time (photo moderation)</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>mc_locale</code></td><td>Remembers whether you chose French or English</td><td>1 year</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>mc_theme</code></td><td>Remembers the colour theme chosen on a scoring tablet</td><td>1 year</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>mc_photo_device</code></td><td>A random number that counts the photos and reports sent from one phone, so a single device cannot flood an event. It does not say who you are</td><td>30 days</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>
<p><strong>This is why you will not see a cookie banner.</strong> A consent banner is required for cookies that are not necessary — advertising, analytics, third-party trackers. MyClash sets none. <code>sb-access-token</code>, <code>sb-refresh-token</code>, <code>mc-oauth-…-code-verifier</code>, <code>mc_guest</code> and <code>mc_staff</code> are strictly necessary for a service you asked for by signing in; <code>mc_photo_device</code> protects the photo sending you are using; <code>mc_locale</code> and <code>mc_theme</code> record a choice you made yourself. Displaying a consent dialog that decides nothing would only teach you to dismiss the ones that matter.</p>
<p>If MyClash ever adds a measurement tool, this section changes and a real consent mechanism will come with it — one that blocks the tool until you agree.</p>

<!-- 10 -->
<h2>10. Security</h2>
<ul>
  <li>All traffic is encrypted in transit (HTTPS/TLS).</li>
  <li>Passwords are never stored in clear text.</li>
  <li>Access to your data is enforced by the database itself, not merely by the application.</li>
  <li>Session cookies are inaccessible to JavaScript, which neutralises an entire class of attack.</li>
  <li>Nightly backups are encrypted and stored off-site; the copy kept before each update stays on our server (§6.1).</li>
  <li>Sign-in attempts are rate-limited, and administrative actions are recorded in an audit trail.</li>
  <li>MyClash is open-source software: its security can be inspected by anyone rather than taken on trust.</li>
</ul>

<!-- 11 -->
<h2>11. Your rights</h2>
<p>Under the GDPR (Articles 15 to 22) you have the following rights. Several are available directly in the application, without waiting for us:</p>
<table>
